                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The condition `err != nil || in.Event != \"\" \u0026\u0026 in.Event != hookwire.EventStop` mixes || and \u0026\u0026 without parentheses. The meaning, that a decode error or an event that is not Stop means nothing to ask, depends on operator precedence and is easy to misread or break in a later edit. Parenthesising the \u0026\u0026 clause or naming it (for example `otherEvent`) would make the intent explicit.",
