            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/cmd/review_stop_hook.go: a command line the hook cannot parse exits 1 before stdin is read. After that, every failure path (unreadable or undecodable input, another event, a missing state home, an unlocatable repository, a store or git error, a panic recovered by the deferred handler) leads to exit 0 with at most one stderr line. Only a ruling with Block set produces stdout output. Exit is called once on each path.",
              "engine/cmd/review_stop_hook.go: stdin is read through a limit of hookwire.MaxEnvelopeBytes+1, and TestReviewStopHookReadsNoMoreOfItsInputThanTheBound asserts the exact byte count read from an endless input.",
              "engine/cmd/review_stop_hook_test.go: tests assert the observable outcomes. They cover the block JSON shape and the next-commit-only reason, once-per-session and per-commit asking, and no use-up of the question on a stop_hook_active continuation. They also cover exemption and blocking-result counting as reviewed, and the default branch, detached HEAD and no-features cases. The no-default-branch block, the missing cwd and session case, and unusable input are covered, as are unreadable state-home and repository errors and the panic. Argument rejection and the usage text are covered too.",
              "engine/cmd/review.go: the change only adds a dispatch case for the new verb. The unknown-verb message is unchanged, so baseline output is preserved.",
              "Minor residual risk, not a defect: if the stdout write fails after the Asked marker is stored, the question is consumed without the agent seeing it. The code comment states that the stop then happens, and nothing in the candidate makes this realistic to hit."
            ]
          }
        }
      }
